---
// Day, sunk. Bridgetown watching prod on its own, as the app shows it: the prod column's API
// 5xx far above its usual level, and the finding Bridgetown raised for it, which no Slack
// alert covered. On a phone, the prod column alone, at a size that reads.
import AppShot from "./AppShot.astro";
import alertWatch from "../assets/app/alert-watch.png";
---

<section class="watch day" id="watch" data-tone="sunk" aria-labelledby="watch-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="chapter-head">
      <h2 id="watch-title" class="display">It watches production, too.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Every five minutes Bridgetown reads your dashboards. When a signal rises well above its usual level and no
        alert covers it, Bridgetown raises a finding of its own and starts an investigation, or suggests one in Needs
        you when Jev doubts it.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="screen">
      <AppShot
        src={alertWatch}
        edge
        alt="Bridgetown open on a finding. Prod: API 5xx at 75, 4.9 times usual, its last bars in amber. The finding: API 5xx at 640 per 5 minutes, usually up to 43. Waiting on you: since 11:45 UTC, API 5xx has been 15 times its usual level for the past 3 hours; merkl-api v1.35.11 deployed at 11:41; no Slack alert has fired for it. No agent has run: Jev suggested one, and it is waiting in Needs you, with an Investigate button."
      />
    </figure>

    <div class="notes">
      <p>
        <b>Rises and spikes.</b> A rise is three steps well above the usual level; a spike is one step far above it.
        A one-step blip never counts, and each signal raises at most one finding every six hours unless it gets three
        times worse.
      </p>
      <p>
        <b>Log patterns.</b> Every ten minutes it groups your logs into patterns, and looks for errors that are new or
        surging and warnings that name a risk: deadlocks, rate limits, retirements.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .watch {
    padding-block: clamp(7rem, 16vh, 11rem);
  }

  .chapter-head .display {
    max-width: 11ch;
  }

  .screen {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .screen :global(.app-shot) {
    box-shadow: 0 30px 60px -36px oklch(0.19 0.008 255 / 0.55);
  }

  .notes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 2rem 4rem;
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 6vh, 4rem);
  }

  .notes p {
    max-width: 34rem;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
  }

  .notes b {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 560;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .notes {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  /* A phone: the prod column, 380 of the screen's 1100 points, cut from its full height. */
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .screen :global(.app-shot) {
      --ratio: 380 / 512;
      --focus: 0 0;
      --radius: 1.25rem;
    }
  }
</style>
